  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper presents three CUDA-Q-simulated gate-based quantum-walk experiments: 1D adaptive distribution generation over NVDA returns and five synthetic distributions, a 5-qubit log-normal option-pricing model on a 16-point grid, and 2D 8x8 digit generation with entangled walkers. The only quantitative benchmark reported is the option-pricing table, where percentage errors range from 3.41% to 19.87% across strikes K=1 to 10; no classical runtime baseline or quantum advantage is demonstrated.",
